2. COMPONENTS AND THEIR LICENCES
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Atari 8-bit core — Mark Watson, (c) 2013-2018
    rtl/common/a8core/*, rtl/common/components/*,
    rtl/common/sioemu/sio_handler.vhdl, plus src/address_decoder.vhdl (a
    modified copy of the upstream address decoder)
    (antic*, gtia*, pokey*, pia, cpu, atari800core*, the shared components and
    the SIO emulation), except the files listed under other headings below.
    Custom non-commercial permission notice — LICENSES/Mark-Watson-NonCommercial.txt
    Upstream: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Atari800_MiSTer

    src/fifo_receive.vhd and src/fifo_transmit.vhd carry no header. They are
    portable replacements for the Altera FIFO wizard files that the upstream
    SIO handler instantiates (same entity names and ports) and are kept with
    the upstream core's terms.

    Several of these files were changed for the Atari816 (classic RAM capped
    at 320 KB in src/address_decoder.vhdl, the paddle simulators and the VBXE
    hook removed, and others); the changes are in the git history and stay
    under the upstream terms.

  Atari palette tables — the NTSC and PAL colour tables in
    rtl/common/a8core/gtia_palette.vhdl are the default palettes of the Altirra
    emulator by Avery Lee (marked "altirra_ntsc_default.pal" /
    "altirra_pal_default.pal" in the file). src/nvc_palette.hex (and its copy
    ../emu/nvc_palette.h) is the same NTSC table. Credit: Avery Lee, Altirra,
    https://www.virtualdub.org/altirra.html

  Upstream Atari800_MiSTer files with NO licence statement
    rtl/common/a8core/internalromram.vhd — no header
    rtl/common/components/mult_infer.vhdl — no header
    These reach us as part of the upstream Atari800_MiSTer tree. No grant
    beyond that tree's terms is claimed for them.

  6502/6510 CPU core — Peter Wendrich (FPGA 64), (c) 2005-2011
    rtl/common/a8core/cpu_65xx.vhd
    Header reads "Copyright 2005-2011 by Peter Wendrich ... All Rights Reserved"
    and carries no licence grant; the file reaches us as part of the upstream
    core above, unchanged. http://www.syntiac.com/fpga64.html

  Cartridge, freezer and PBI logic — Matthias Reichl, (c) 2011-2014,
  and Wojciech Mostowski, (c) 2025
    rtl/common/a8core/cart_logic.vhd, rtl/common/a8core/freezer_logic.vhd,
    rtl/common/a8core/pbi_rom.vhdl
    GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2 or later — LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt
    cart_logic.vhd is modified here (reduced to the common bank-switching
    schemes for the Atari816; the notice is in the file) and stays LGPL.

  IO subsystem (PicoRV32 host, SPI peripherals) — nand2mario
    src/iosys_picorv32.v, src/simplespimaster.v, src/spiflash.v
    Adapted from nand2mario's NESTang/SNESTang — GNU General Public License v3.0
    LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt
    Upstream: https://github.com/nand2mario/nestang (COPYING = GPL-3.0)

  Simple UART — Claire Xenia Wolf, (c) 2017 (PicoSoC)
    src/simpleuart.v — ISC licence, in the file header.
    Upstream: https://github.com/YosysHQ/picorv32

  SPI master (byte-level, i_TX_DV / o_TX_Ready interface)
    src/spi_master.v — no copyright or licence header. Its description and
    port names match the nandland SPI master (Russell Merrick, MIT licence,
    https://github.com/nandland/spi-master). This attribution is UNVERIFIED.

  PicoRV32 CPU core — Claire Xenia Wolf, (c) 2015
    src/picorv32.v — ISC licence, in the file header.
    Upstream: https://github.com/YosysHQ/picorv32

  SD-card firmware base (firmware/) — nand2mario
